## 6. Compliance [CYD-CAPTURE-COMPLIANCE]

### [CYD-CAP-C1] Capture produces a valid 24-bit BMP file readable by standard image viewers
### [CYD-CAP-C2] Band buffer is reused — no additional framebuffer allocation during capture
### [CYD-CAP-C3] BMP is written to SD card, not held in memory
### [CYD-CAP-C4] WiFi PUT sends the BMP to document_store and receives 200/201
### [CYD-CAP-C5] BMP is deleted from SD after successful push
### [CYD-CAP-C6] Capture does not crash or corrupt the display render loop
### [CYD-CAP-C7] RGB565 to RGB888 conversion preserves color accuracy (5-6-5 bit replication)

